## Engineering assistance — Claude AI (Anthropic)

Significant portions of this project were developed in collaboration with
**Claude** (Anthropic's AI assistant), used as an engineering partner
throughout the design, documentation, and research phases.

Specifically, Claude was used to:

- Research components, suppliers, and alternative parts
- Generate first drafts of technical documentation (datasheets, guides,
  pinout references, bring-up procedures)
- Review schematics and identify potential issues
- Plan project structure and file organization
- Draft commit messages and pull request descriptions
- Help organize the configurator's grblHAL settings generator logic
- Maintain a persistent memory of project context across development sessions

**All final design decisions, hardware choices, component selections,
business decisions, and architectural choices were made by Filip Perić.**

Claude served as a fast research, drafting, and review partner — not as
a decision-maker. The judgment, hands-on experience, and ownership of
the project remain entirely with the human author.

This acknowledgment is intentionally transparent. Open hardware deserves
open process disclosure.


